# Allow-list: only the files behind the current version of the article are tracked -- the code it
# runs, the tests, and the result files, logs, figures and tables it reports. Everything else
# (earlier versions, the manuscript source, caches) is ignored. Trained checkpoints and raw data
# are release assets (scripts/release_assets.py, checkpoints/README.md, data/README.md).
# Add a new file here explicitly.
*
!.gitignore

